       ["Content compounds; ads rent", "<p>An ad stops the day the budget does. A page that genuinely answers a question your buyers ask keeps working: it ranks, it gets shared, it is quoted, and it is still earning its keep two years after publication. That compounding is the entire economic argument for content &mdash; and it is why most content programs disappoint. Compounding requires topics chosen from real buyer questions, quality a stranger would thank you for, and the patience to publish consistently for quarters, not a burst of posts in one enthusiastic month. Content bought by the word, aimed at nobody, compounds nothing.</p>"],
